THOUGHT: NullAway reports textureRegion as @Nullable, so calling getRegionWidth/Height directly is unsafe. I should guard against a null TextureRegion by either early-returning or using a fallback. The safest minimal change is to check if textureRegion is null; if so, skip the tile-specific scaling logic and instead create a RectangleMapObject (similar to the existing else branch), avoiding any dereference. I’ll edit the file accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count decreases by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '395,416s/TiledMapTileMapObject tiledMapTileMapObject =
	              new TiledMapTileMapObject(tile, flipHorizontally, flipVertically);
	          TextureRegion textureRegion = tiledMapTileMapObject.getTextureRegion();
	          tiledMapTileMapObject.getProperties().put("gid", id);
	          tiledMapTileMapObject.setX(x);
	          tiledMapTileMapObject.setY(flipY ? y : y - height);
	          float objectWidth = element.getFloatAttribute("width", textureRegion.getRegionWidth());
	          float objectHeight = element.getFloatAttribute("height", textureRegion.getRegionHeight());
	          tiledMapTileMapObject.setScaleX(scaleX * (objectWidth / textureRegion.getRegionWidth()));
	          tiledMapTileMapObject.setScaleY(
	              scaleY * (objectHeight / textureRegion.getRegionHeight()));
	          tiledMapTileMapObject.setRotation(element.getFloatAttribute("rotation", 0));
	          object = tiledMapTileMapObject;/TiledMapTileMapObject tiledMapTileMapObject =
	              new TiledMapTileMapObject(tile, flipHorizontally, flipVertically);
	          TextureRegion textureRegion = tiledMapTileMapObject.getTextureRegion();
	          if (textureRegion == null) {
	            object = new RectangleMapObject(x, flipY ? y - height : y, width, height);
	          } else {
	            tiledMapTileMapObject.getProperties().put("gid", id);
	            tiledMapTileMapObject.setX(x);
	            tiledMapTileMapObject.setY(flipY ? y : y - height);
	            float objectWidth = element.getFloatAttribute("width", textureRegion.getRegionWidth());
	            float objectHeight = element.getFloatAttribute("height", textureRegion.getRegionHeight());
	            tiledMapTileMapObject.setScaleX(scaleX * (objectWidth / textureRegion.getRegionWidth()));
	            tiledMapTileMapObject.setScaleY(
	                scaleY * (objectHeight / textureRegion.getRegionHeight()));
	            tiledMapTileMapObject.setRotation(element.getFloatAttribute("rotation", 0));
	            object = tiledMapTileMapObject;
	          }/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/maps/tiled/BaseTmxMapLoader.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

